{{! See Also references (@see, @sa).

    Overrides the stock template, which renders each entry as its own paragraph.
    The entries render as a bulleted list, as elsewhere in the documentation.
    The bullets cannot come from the doc comment: `@see` takes a paragraph
    argument, and a list written there collapses onto a single line.

    The bullet is written here rather than through `markup/li`, because the item
    has to end in exactly one newline: none and the entries run together, two
    and Markdown treats the list as loose and wraps every item in a paragraph.
}}
{{#if symbol.doc.sees}}
{{#> markup/section name="see-also"}}
{{#> markup/dynamic-level-h }}See Also{{/markup/dynamic-level-h~}}
{{#each symbol.doc.sees}}
- {{> doc/block/see .}}
{{/each}}
{{/markup/section}}
{{/if}}
